title ALES18 — Lotus's live loop meter, a looping stereo region read under two meters
prompt Autonomous loop past REMEMBER + the itineraries — take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment, stop at the custody gates.
think ALES17 (stereo meter during forward playback) landed and its own road-on named the next want plainly: meter a LOOPING stereo region live — ALES16's wrap under the ALES17 meter. Crux-first: composing the two most recent proven rungs (the wrapping head + the two-channel meter) is the highest-Lindy, most-tractable move — no new arithmetic, only the recognition that they already fit, closing the read side's stereo arc (play·loop·meter) into a freely-composing whole. A punch region would cross into the Mikrophone capture side (a module seam per collaboration.md — check-in Claude), so I deliberately did NOT take it.
think The crux and why it is EXACT, not merely close: metering a whole number of cycles gives the identical per-channel peak and RMS as metering the region once at rest. Peak is a max, invariant under repetition. RMS is a mean square, whose sum_sq and count both scale by the cycle count K, and the common factor cancels EXACTLY even under integer floor division — @divTrunc(K·S, K·N) == @divTrunc(S, N), since K·S/(K·N) = S/N as rationals and the floor of an unchanged rational is unchanged. So the live loop VU is stable across cycle count for free, on ALES13's one true isqrt.
think Reuse over reinvention: stereo_meter.StereoMeter/feed/peak_*/rms_* reused whole; stereo_loop.read_block + loop.enter drive the wrapping read; the only new code is measure_region (the at-rest reference), meter_loop_live (the live driver reading exactly cycles×span samples), and the cycle bound. The bound doubles as the overflow guard: cycles > @divTrunc(max_meter_samples, span) refuses MeterFull before the u32 product is formed.
think First build failed — reached stereo_transport through stereo_meter.stereo_transport, which is not pub. Fixed by importing stereo_transport.rye directly for the LoopMeterError set. Second build GREEN.
obs GREEN on the second build: block-and-cycle invariance at 1/2/5-sample blocks and 1,3,7 cycles matched measure_region exactly per channel; 100 cycles read the same peak and RMS as one (the human payoff — a steady practice-loop VU); a loud left (square wave 8000) and quiet right (spike 100) read distinct levels off the live loop; a power-rendered center pan loops-and-meters 700 per side; neither channel mutated after six cycles; the cycle count refused MeterFull past ALES13's bound.
obs tame_style_check exit 0 (bans clean); the new module carries many asserts, off the zero-assert ratchet.
loom witness=ales_stereo_loop_meter_witness cases=6 blocks=3 cycles=3 result=GREEN build=second-try
file lotus/stereo_loop_meter.rye ALES18 module — the live loop meter, ALES16's wrapping head fed into ALES17's two meters.
file tools/ales_stereo_loop_meter_witness.rish the witness proving ALES18 GREEN on metal.
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales18-lotus-stereo-loop-meter.md the self-approved design round for ALES18.
file lotus/README.md status line, rung bullet, and road-on updated for ALES18.
recommend keep-going ALES19 can name a scrub window (a small movable read across a mono or stereo master) or offer the keeper the choice of pan/crossfade law on either axis — both agent-doable, no custody gate. A punch region tying playback to the Mikrophone's capture is a module seam that waits for Keaton's word.
